      "tag": "div",
      "text": "Here is the beautiful neuroscience behind the sadness of something ending:When you’re in the middle of a pleasurable experience, dopamine is driving the “wanting it to keep going” feeling via a series of anticipatory spikes. Even while you’re having it! When it ends, that anticipation is left hanging and a dopamine dip ensues. This doesn’t feel great — deprivation, sadness, perhaps a bit of wistfulness. But it passes.",
      "visible": true
    },
